# ==============================================================================
# THE DOCUMENTS THIS PROJECT BUILDS (the pandoc pack)
# ==============================================================================
# What `gmake pdf_from_md`, `gmake docx_from_md` and `gmake pdf_open` read.
# `gmake env_project_enable` copies this block into the project's .env the first time
# it runs; after that it only adds what is missing, so a value you filled in is
# never overwritten.
#
# The four lines stay commented out on purpose - a commented line does not
# travel into the .env, and leaving it out means "unset, and the target
# decides". A project with one markdown file and the template called
# template.tex says nothing here and everything works.
#
# Nothing reads this file: it is a sample. The project's .env is what gmake
# loads.
# ==============================================================================

# --- The markdown to build, when the project holds several ---
# Example: PDF_SRC=rapport.md
#PDF_SRC=

# --- What to write, when the derived names are not the ones you want ---
# Example: PDF_OUT=rapport-rv.pdf
#PDF_OUT=
# Example: DOCX_OUT=rapport-rv.docx
#DOCX_OUT=

# --- The template, when the project's is not template.tex ---
# Example: PDF_TEMPLATE=templates/rapport.tex
#PDF_TEMPLATE=

# --- The Word file's look: a .docx whose styles pandoc copies ---
# Example: DOCX_REFERENCE=templates/modele.docx
#DOCX_REFERENCE=
